[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
To set up Gitea Runner, follow https://gitea.com/gitea/runner, but put
its config in %%ETCDIR%%/config.yaml, readable by group
%%GITEA_RUNNER_GROUP%%, and register it like this, so that it reads that config
and the .runner file it writes is not readable by everyone:

  cd /var/db/gitea-runner
  su -m %%GITEA_RUNNER_USER%% -c 'umask 027 && %%PREFIX%%/bin/gitea-runner \
    -c %%ETCDIR%%/config.yaml register'

To start it, enable it, create its log file, and have syslogd pick up
its log settings:

  sysrc gitea_runner_enable=YES
  newsyslog -CN /var/log/gitea-runner.log
  service syslogd reload
  service gitea_runner start

The runner logs to /var/log/gitea-runner.log. Its output also appears
in /var/log/daemon.log, because /etc/syslog.conf sends daemon.info
there.

Unless all of its labels are host labels, such as freebsd:host, the
runner runs jobs in containers and needs a Docker-compatible API, such
as Podman's. Host jobs need it too, for Docker actions. For Podman,
give the runner's group Podman's socket with podman_service_api_group,
restart podman_service, and set container.docker_host to "-" in the
config: the socket gives control of root's Podman, and otherwise every
job container gets it.

To run more than one runner, see gitea_runner_profiles in
%%PREFIX%%/etc/rc.d/gitea_runner.
EOM
}
]
